Lua 5.5.1 development library for Pyxis

The upstream MIT notice is retained in lua.h. source.txt records the exact
upstream commit and ordered patches. The archive contains Lua's core and the
upstream standard libraries, including math, debug and the stock initializer. The interpreter's native Pyxis module and job helpers are separate
objects and are not part of liblua.a. The interpreter's SHA-256 helper therefore does not
add a crypto dependency to this development library.

Upstream-derived patches retain Lua's MIT terms. The forced-include config.h,
recipe and packaging metadata are original Pyxis material under MPL-2.0.
The configuration's preferred source is retained under share/sources/lua/;
MPL-2.0 and LICENSING.md accompany this notice. The installed upstream headers
declare APIs beyond the selected profile; installation is not qualification of
every upstream API.
